# Parameter Template Pattern

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides a standardized template pattern for creating project-rule-parameter documentation. It should be used when creating new parameter files to ensure consistency, completeness, and compliance with documentation standards.

## Parameter Documentation Template

Use this template as the foundation for all parameter documentation:

```markdown
# Parameter Name

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file serves as a project-rule-parameter for [specific purpose]. It provides [functionality/guidance] for [use case] and should be used when [conditions].

This file complements:
- [Related file 1]: [Relationship description]
- [Related file 2]: [Relationship description]

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

```
message-command: @parameters/workflow/category/parameter-name.mdc
```

Optional parameters:
- `param1`: [Description of param1]
- `param2`: [Description of param2]

## [Main Content Section]

[Detailed content appropriate to the parameter's purpose]

## Implementation Guidelines

1. [Step 1 of implementation]
2. [Step 2 of implementation]
3. [Step 3 of implementation]

Important considerations:
- [Consideration 1]
- [Consideration 2]

## Examples

### Basic Usage
```
message-command: @parameters/workflow/category/parameter-name.mdc
```

### Advanced Usage
```
message-command: param1="value1" param2="value2" @parameters/workflow/category/parameter-name.mdc
```

## File Standard Notice

This file follows the standard project-rule-parameter format with appropriate sections for usage documentation. USE WHEN [specific usage context].
```

## Template Section Descriptions

### Header (Required)

```markdown
# Parameter Name
```

- Use the exact parameter name in title case
- Should match the filename (without extension)
- Should clearly indicate the parameter's purpose

### File Purpose and Relationship (Required)

```markdown
## File Purpose and Relationship

This file serves as a project-rule-parameter for [specific purpose]. It provides [functionality/guidance] for [use case] and should be used when [conditions].

This file complements:
- [Related file 1]: [Relationship description]
- [Related file 2]: [Relationship description]
```

- Clearly state the parameter's purpose
- Explain when to use this parameter
- List related files and how they complement this parameter
- Keep this section concise (3-5 sentences plus related files)

### Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter (Required)

```markdown
## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

```
message-command: @parameters/workflow/category/parameter-name.mdc
```

Optional parameters:
- `param1`: [Description of param1]
- `param2`: [Description of param2]
```

- Show the exact syntax for using the parameter
- List all optional parameters with descriptions
- Use the exact path that matches the file structure
- Use code blocks for command examples

### Main Content Sections (Parameter-Specific)

```markdown
## [Main Content Section]

[Detailed content appropriate to the parameter's purpose]
```

- Include sections specific to the parameter's purpose
- Use descriptive headers for each section
- Organize content logically
- Use lists, tables, and code blocks as appropriate

### Implementation Guidelines (Required)

```markdown
## Implementation Guidelines

1. [Step 1 of implementation]
2. [Step 2 of implementation]
3. [Step 3 of implementation]

Important considerations:
- [Consideration 1]
- [Consideration 2]
```

- Provide step-by-step implementation guidance
- Include important considerations or warnings
- Focus on practical implementation details
- Use numbered lists for sequential steps

### Examples (Required)

```markdown
## Examples

### Basic Usage
```
message-command: @parameters/workflow/category/parameter-name.mdc
```

### Advanced Usage
```
message-command: param1="value1" param2="value2" @parameters/workflow/category/parameter-name.mdc
```
```

- Include at least one basic example
- Add advanced examples if applicable
- Use code blocks for all examples
- Provide context for each example

### File Standard Notice (Required)

```markdown
## File Standard Notice

This file follows the standard project-rule-parameter format with appropriate sections for usage documentation. USE WHEN [specific usage context].
```

- Include this exact notice format
- Customize only the USE WHEN section
- Be specific about when to use this parameter
- Keep the USE WHEN statement concise

